# Febris Node -- local TLS front for the clone-and-run compose stack.
#
# WHY A PROXY AT ALL: the portal's auth cookie is SecurePolicy=Always + SameSite=None -- login
# simply cannot work over plain HTTP, so a working HTTPS entry point is part of clone-and-run.
#
# local_certs = Caddy's own self-signed local CA (no ACME, no internet). Your browser will warn
# once; accept it for the trial, or trust the CA (SELF_HOSTING.md). *.localhost hostnames
# resolve to loopback in modern browsers with no /etc/hosts edit.
#
# HSTS note: the hosts emit HSTS themselves. The febris.localhost names keep that pin OFF the
# bare "localhost" host, so this stack never force-upgrades your other local dev servers.
#
# PRODUCTION: replace both site addresses with your real domains (and drop local_certs) --
# Caddy then provisions publicly-trusted certificates via ACME automatically.

{
	local_certs
}

# THE PROBE ENDPOINTS ARE NOT PUBLIC.
#
# /health/live and /health/ready are deliberately AllowAnonymous, because an orchestrator probe
# cannot authenticate, and that is correct. What was wrong was letting them out through this proxy.
# Both hosts map them (FebrisEndUserApi/Startup.cs and FebrisEndUserPortal/Startup.cs), and each
# vhost below forwarded its whole path space, so /health/ready was reachable from anywhere the
# stack was. The readiness body names every registered check, so an unauthenticated caller could
# enumerate which databases the node owns, whether Redis is configured, whether hub federation is
# on, and watch dependency health live. Harmless on a *.localhost trial, and this file's own
# PRODUCTION note tells operators to swap in real domains, at which point it is not.
#
# NOTHING LEGITIMATE LOSES ACCESS. The container healthchecks run INSIDE each container
# (`curl http://localhost/health/ready`, docker-compose.yml) and never traverse Caddy, and the API
# publishes a loopback-only port so the host can still curl the probes directly.
#
# 404 rather than 403 on purpose: a refusal confirms the endpoint is there.
(no_public_probes) {
	@probes path /health/*
	respond @probes 404
}

# The operator portal.
https://febris.localhost:8443 {
	import no_public_probes

	reverse_proxy node-portal:80 {
		# The analytics middlewares read X-Real-IP when UsingRevProxy=true; Caddy sets
		# X-Forwarded-* on its own.
		header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
	}
}

# The node API (xAPI ingest, launcher/mobile endpoints).
https://api.febris.localhost:8443 {
	import no_public_probes

	reverse_proxy node-api:80 {
		header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
	}
}
